# Naamalu Design System

**Read `docs/design-system.md` before writing or editing UI code.** It is the canonical source for tokens, typography, components, and Compose structure.

Stack: Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, Android-only. Aesthetic: **reverent, restrained, text-first** — the sacred name is the hero; UI chrome recedes.

## Non-negotiables

1. Use `NaamaluTheme.colors` — never `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` for brand tokens.
2. Render all divine names via `SacredName(text, script)` — script-aware Noto Serif; never Inter, never clip/ellipsize.
3. Gold (`#C79A3E`) is hairlines/dividers only — never fills or large surfaces.
4. Streaks and missed days use `muted` — never red/error styling.
5. No gradients, glows, or heavy drop shadows; prefer `0.dp` elevation + hairline borders.
6. Themes: **Dina** (light) and **Ratri** (dark); access via `NaamaluTheme`.

## Theme files (expected layout)

- `ui/theme/Color.kt`, `NaamaluColors.kt`, `Type.kt`, `Theme.kt`

When adding colors, components, or type styles, update `docs/design-system.md` in the same change.
